<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<MachineRuntimeConfiguration xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ConfigurationName>Standalone IO Template</ConfigurationName>
  <ConfigurationVersion>1.0</ConfigurationVersion>
  <LastUpdatedUtc>2026-03-16T00:00:00Z</LastUpdatedUtc>
  <DigitalIoBoard>PCIE-1756-BE</DigitalIoBoard>
  <EncoderBoard>PCIE-1884-AE</EncoderBoard>
  <TriggerMode>Hybrid</TriggerMode>
  <RejectMode>EncoderTracked</RejectMode>
  <Notes>Configurable camera I/O template: photocell starts product tracking, encoder/virtual conveyor advances position, DO02 triggers TOP, DO01 triggers SIDE/LEFT, DO04 triggers REAR/RIGHT, DO05 triggers BOTTOM. DO00 is intentionally spare unless explicitly configured for diagnostics.</Notes>
  <MachineInputs>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>IN_PRODUCT_PHOTOCELL</SignalCode>
      <Description>Photocell detecting product passage</Description>
      <Direction>Input</Direction>
      <Category>PresenceSensor</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DI00</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Master event for product tracking.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>IN_EXTERNAL_TRIGGER_ENABLE</SignalCode>
      <Description>External trigger enable</Description>
      <Direction>Input</Direction>
      <Category>CameraTrigger</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DI01</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Used when camera shot is commanded by external logic.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
  </MachineInputs>
  <MachineOutputs>
   
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_SIDE_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <Description>Camera Side hardware trigger pulse</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>CameraTrigger</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO01</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Real trigger output for side camera and related illuminator enable chain.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_TOP_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <Description>Camera Top hardware trigger pulse</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>CameraTrigger</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO02</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Real trigger output for top camera and related illuminator enable chain.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_REJECT_SOLENOID</SignalCode>
      <Description>Reject actuator command</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>Reject</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO03</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Mono reject output.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_REAR_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <Description>Camera Rear/Right hardware trigger pulse</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>CameraTrigger</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO04</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Optional trigger output for rear camera used as right-side complementary view.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_BOTTOM_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <Description>Camera Bottom hardware trigger pulse</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>CameraTrigger</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO05</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Optional trigger output for bottom camera. Can be single-shot or MultiShot according to machine setup.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_GENERAL_ALARM</SignalCode>
      <Description>General fault output to stack light or PLC</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>Alarm</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO06</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>true</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Dedicated to blocking machine alarms.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
    <MachineSignalDefinition>
      <SignalCode>OUT_HEARTBEAT</SignalCode>
      <Description>Diagnostic heartbeat output for commissioning and board communication test</Description>
      <Direction>Output</Direction>
      <Category>Alarm</Category>
      <Board>PCIE-1756-BE</Board>
      <Channel>DO07</Channel>
      <Polarity>ActiveHigh</Polarity>
      <ReservedForRealSignal>false</ReservedForRealSignal>
      <Notes>Dedicated blinking output for diagnostics. Prefer a spare channel or commissioning lamp.</Notes>
    </MachineSignalDefinition>
  </MachineOutputs>
  <EncoderTemplates>
    <EncoderConfigurationTemplate>
      <AxisName>ENC_CONVEYOR_MAIN</AxisName>
      <Board>PCIE-1884-AE</Board>
      <Channel>Counter0</Channel>
      <PulsesPerRevolution>2048</PulsesPerRevolution>
      <MillimetersPerRevolution>100</MillimetersPerRevolution>
      <MachineZeroLabel>INIZIO_TRASPORTO</MachineZeroLabel>
      <PhotocellMachineOffsetMm>35.5</PhotocellMachineOffsetMm>
      <TrackingMode>Quadrature x4</TrackingMode>
      <TriggerOffsetMm>0</TriggerOffsetMm>
      <RejectOffsetMm>350</RejectOffsetMm>
      <Notes>Main conveyor reference. In virtual-conveyor mode product tracking starts from the photocell at 35.5 mm from machine zero.</Notes>
    </EncoderConfigurationTemplate>
  </EncoderTemplates>
  <InterventionPoints>
    <MachineInterventionPoint>
      <PointCode>CAMERA_TRIGGER_TOP</PointCode>
      <Description>Trigger camera top</Description>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ReferenceCode>PRODUCT_ZERO</ReferenceCode>
      <BaseOffsetMm>74</BaseOffsetMm>
      <TrimOffsetMm>0</TrimOffsetMm>
      <ActionType>TriggerCamera</ActionType>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_TOP_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <PulseMs>40</PulseMs>
      <IsStandard>true</IsStandard>
      <Notes>Pulse TOP camera trigger at 74.0 mm from PRODUCT_ZERO. External wiring may use the same pulse to enable the illuminator.</Notes>
    </MachineInterventionPoint>
    <MachineInterventionPoint>
      <PointCode>CAMERA_TRIGGER_SIDE</PointCode>
      <Description>Trigger camera side</Description>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ReferenceCode>PRODUCT_ZERO</ReferenceCode>
      <BaseOffsetMm>76</BaseOffsetMm>
      <TrimOffsetMm>0</TrimOffsetMm>
      <ActionType>TriggerCamera</ActionType>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_SIDE_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <PulseMs>40</PulseMs>
      <IsStandard>true</IsStandard>
      <Notes>Pulse SIDE camera trigger at 76.0 mm from PRODUCT_ZERO. External wiring may use the same pulse to enable the illuminator.</Notes>
    </MachineInterventionPoint>
    <MachineInterventionPoint>
      <PointCode>REJECT</PointCode>
      <Description>Reject intervention point</Description>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ReferenceCode>PRODUCT_ZERO</ReferenceCode>
      <BaseOffsetMm>350</BaseOffsetMm>
      <TrimOffsetMm>0</TrimOffsetMm>
      <ActionType>Reject</ActionType>
      <SignalCode>OUT_REJECT_SOLENOID</SignalCode>
      <PulseMs>80</PulseMs>
      <IsStandard>true</IsStandard>
      <Notes>Activates reject only for NOK products when they reach the real machine position.</Notes>
    </MachineInterventionPoint>
    <MachineInterventionPoint>
      <PointCode>CAMERA_TRIGGER_REAR</PointCode>
      <Description>Trigger camera rear/right</Description>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ReferenceCode>PRODUCT_ZERO</ReferenceCode>
      <BaseOffsetMm>76</BaseOffsetMm>
      <TrimOffsetMm>0</TrimOffsetMm>
      <ActionType>TriggerCamera</ActionType>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_REAR_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <PulseMs>40</PulseMs>
      <IsStandard>true</IsStandard>
      <Notes>Pulse REAR/RIGHT camera trigger at the configured product position. For MultiShot this point defines the first shot position.</Notes>
    </MachineInterventionPoint>
    <MachineInterventionPoint>
      <PointCode>CAMERA_TRIGGER_BOTTOM</PointCode>
      <Description>Trigger camera bottom</Description>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ReferenceCode>PRODUCT_ZERO</ReferenceCode>
      <BaseOffsetMm>76</BaseOffsetMm>
      <TrimOffsetMm>0</TrimOffsetMm>
      <ActionType>TriggerCamera</ActionType>
      <SignalCode>OUT_CAMERA_BOTTOM_TRIGGER</SignalCode>
      <PulseMs>40</PulseMs>
      <IsStandard>true</IsStandard>
      <Notes>Pulse BOTTOM camera trigger at the configured product position. Can remain single-shot or be owned by the Bottom MultiShot profile.</Notes>
    </MachineInterventionPoint>
  </InterventionPoints>
  <RuntimeBindings>
